<title>AUSTRALIA: JB Were says still has 10.25 pct of PMP.</title>
<headline>JB Were says still has 10.25 pct of PMP.</headline>
<dateline>SYDNEY 1996-07-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Stockbroker J.B. Were Group Holdings Ltd said in a substantial shareholding notice to the Australian Stock Exchange it had cut its stake in magazine and multi-media group PMP Communications Ltd to 10.25 pecent from 40.5 percent.</p>
<p>JB Were bought 101.6 million PMP shares from News on Tuesday and was thought to have traded the stake on to institutional investors, but other brokers had speculated JB Were had been unable to sell all the stake immediately.</p>
<p>PMP shares closed up five cents at A$3.24 on Thursday.</p>
<p>-- Sydney Newsroom 61-2 9373-1800</p>
</text>
